{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-330627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide each term of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{7\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-7 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =7 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{7}{2})≈1.292\\,50\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}≈1.292\\,50+\\pi ≈4.434\\,09\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.29,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.43.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.29"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330627" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4.43"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 3\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{4}{3})=-0.927\\,295\\,218…≈-0.927\\,295\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to 6 decimal places. \n\nSince $-0.927\\,295$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+\\pi ≈2.214\\,297 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\pi +x=-0.927\\,295…+2\\pi ≈5.355\\,890\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈2.214\\,297\\cdot 5.355\\,890≈11.860\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10.859"] ["math" "11.860"] ["math" "15.685"] ["math" "16.850"] ["math" "18.816"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11.860"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order**, rounded to two decimal places in radians, the solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ are\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n {{field-1}}$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =\\frac{8\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{8}{3})≈1.212\\,03\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\nx≈1.212\\,03+\\pi ≈4.353\\,62\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places. \n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to two decimal places, the solutions are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}≈1.21,\\,{x}_{2}≈4.35.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.21"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-330495" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4.35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=x+2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{11\\pi }{6}=\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{36\\pi }{55}"] ["math" "\\frac{36{\\pi }^{2}}{55}"] ["math" "\\frac{55\\pi }{36}"] ["math" "\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}"] ["math" "\\frac{6\\pi }{55}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-21607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{55{\\pi }^{2}}{36}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{5\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-5 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})=1.190\\,289\\,949…≈1.190\\,290\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nSince $1.190\\,290$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.190\\,290.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +1.190\\,289\\,949…=4.331\\,882\\,603\\,…≈4.331\\,883\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈1.190\\,290\\cdot 4.331\\,883≈5.156\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4.156"] ["math" "5.062"] ["math" "5.156"] ["math" "5.250"] ["math" "5.306"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8831" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5.156"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{6\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-6 & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6)≈{80.538}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${80.538}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={80.538}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we subtract ${180}^{∘}$ from the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={80.538}^{∘}-{180}^{∘}≈-{99.462}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $80.538\\cdot (-99.462)≈-8\\,010.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6\\,487"] ["math" "-8\\,000"] ["math" "-8\\,010"] ["math" "-9\\,000"] ["math" "-9\\,892"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-122673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8\\,010"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+\\frac{4\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+4 & =0 \\\\ 8\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-0.463\\,647…≈-0.463\\,65\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nSince $-0.463\\,65$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.463\\,65.$\n\nTo find the other solution, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-0.463\\,65…+\\pi ≈2.677\\,95\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈-0.463\\,65\\cdot 2.677\\,95≈-1.24\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/state.json" "file_sha256" "075d962bdfee6120ce273fa5867c4a455fd56fc6cb6cbba4393a6e1804358218"} {"question" "q-8873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055789/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e05b472e59b38af60f68a33e9dc089a91f10ae2595716a52efa34b80fcb2f832"} {"question" "q-8873" "field" 